<urn:atm:triage:finding/AG19-RBQA-F003>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AG19-RBQA-F003" ;
  triage:title "Divergent outcome-classification for Deferred/OutcomeUnknown between ack-reply and daemon dispatch paths" ;
  triage:description "atm-daemon's dispatch_send (crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health/dispatch_delivery.rs:75-94) treats RemoteSendDeliveryOutcome::Deferred/OutcomeUnknown as non-error Sent(Deferred) outcomes: Ok(send_sent_response(build_remote_deferred_outcome(...))), preserving receipt_message_id for graceful deferred handling. atm-core's execute_ack_reply_plan (crates/atm-core/src/ack/mod.rs:686-687) treats the identical variants as hard Err(error), discarding receipt_message_id and failing the ack-reply operation. Confirmed functionally unchanged at bf96dc86 despite arch-ctm's claim of fix. Regression introduced AG.19 (commit 59225e0f), carried forward unchanged through AG.20 and AG.21. Fix prescription: restore Ok-with-warnings semantics for Deferred/OutcomeUnknown in ack/mod.rs, matching dispatch_delivery.rs behavior (or route through shared helper). Severity upgraded to CRITICAL per rust-service-hardening-agent assessment (QA-2 recheck). Note: RSH-001 consolidated into this record (same defect, different reviewer pathway)." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AG" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "repeatable sweep AG.19-AG.21 for any other divergent Deferred/OutcomeUnknown handling between daemon dispatch and ack/mod.rs -- sweep of feature/pAG-s21-collapse-dispatch-routing found no additional divergent RemoteSendDeliveryOutcome match sites beyond the one described here (dispatch_delivery.rs, ack/mod.rs execute_ack_reply_plan, and non_claude_outbound_runtime.rs construction site all reviewed; only ack/mod.rs diverges)" ;
  triage:category "correctness" ;
  triage:severity "critical" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-19T12:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AG19-RBQA-F003/pAG-s19/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AG19-RBQA-F003/pAG-s20/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AG19-RBQA-F003/pAG-s21/1> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAG-s19/59225e0f> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAG-s20/50572166> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAG-s21/bf96dc86> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAG-s21/bf96dc86> ;
  triage:crossReference "RSH-001 consolidated into this record (followup_pass QA-2 recheck confirms same defect: unfixed despite arch-ctm claim). AG20-BLOCK-002 (transport-owned deferred/outcome-unknown policy on feature/pAG-s20-move-deferred-policy-out-of-transport) is the same class of defect -- same repeatable pattern (divergent-outcome-classification): outcome-classification logic re-implemented instead of shared. Both findings should be resolved together on AG.21 since it is the branch actively collapsing dispatch routing." ;
  triage:notes "FOLLOWUP_PASS RECHECK (QA-2 @ bf96dc86): Defect still present and functionally unchanged. Commit bf96dc86 titled 'AG.21 collapse remote outcome policy and fail closed ack' did NOT fix the divergence: still has hard Err(error) for Deferred/OutcomeUnknown in ack/mod.rs:686-687, divergent from dispatch_delivery.rs:75-94 which treats them as Ok(Sent(Deferred)). arch-ctm's claimed fix was not committed. Consolidated RSH-001 (rust-service-hardening-agent finding of same defect) into this record. Severity upgraded from 'blocking' to 'critical' per RSH-001's rust-service-hardening-agent rating. dispatch_ready = false because defect is unfixed and unresolved at highest-open branch (bf96dc86). highest_open_branch = feature/pAG-s21-collapse-dispatch-routing (bf96dc86). promote_to_branch = same." .

